{"raw": {"https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/environmental-services-worker-housekeeping": {"title": "ENVIRONMENTAL SERVICES WORKER (Housekeeping)", "description": "ENVIRONMENTAL SERVICES WORKER (Housekeeping) - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall ENVIRONMENTAL SERVICES WORKER (Housekeeping) Openings are dayshift (M-F), but may require some flexibility for occasional evenings and weekends.   This is a great role for working parents as shifts start early in the morning and end in the early afternoon. Thiel College offers a robust benefits package, including tuition remission.  Our engaging campus community is a family-friendly place to work as we support a safe, functional, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. We are currently seeking full-time Environmental Services Workers.  Our Environmental Service Workers are responsible for performing various day-to-day housekeeping services including, but not limited to, sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, waxing floors, cleaning restrooms, and dusting in academic, event, and residential spaces, as well as performing any other reasonable duties as assigned. Qualifications: Preferred: Customer Service Skills Professional,      confidential, and positive personality Previous housekeeping      experience is preferred. Must also be able to lift,      push or pull up to 50 pounds; Working conditions require      standing, bending, kneeling, use of stairs and ladders, and use of      protective clothing/equipment. Required: A      post-job-offer physical exam, drug screening and background check will be      required (scheduled and paid by the College). For further information, please contact Decwin Waite, Assistant Director of Environmental Services, at dwaite@thiel.edu . Why Thiel? Thiel College empowers individuals to reach their full potential by creating a diverse and inclusive learning environment that ensures educational excellence, stimulates global awareness, and promotes ethical leadership. In doing so, Thiel prepares students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should submit an application by clicking here . Any additional application materials should be attached in a single PDF document using candidate\u2019s last name as the document title. Materials will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/mens-lacrosse-head-coach": {"title": "Head Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach", "description": "Head Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Head Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach Thiel College seeks an innovative and energetic Head Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach to lead and advance its NCAA Division III Men\u2019s lacrosse program. This is a full-time, 12-month position that reports directly to the Director of Athletics. The successful candidate will provide vision, leadership, and oversight for all aspects of the lacrosse program while supporting Thiel\u2019s mission and holistic student development. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Direct and oversee all aspects of the Men\u2019s lacrosse program, including daily operations, practice planning, and game preparation. Serve as teacher, mentor, and role model for student-athletes in alignment with Thiel\u2019s mission and values. Recruit, retain, and graduate quality student-athletes while consistently meeting or exceeding established roster goals. Develop and implement a strategic recruiting plan that enhances the program\u2019s visibility and competitiveness. Monitor academic performance, social behavior, and personal growth of student-athletes. Build and maintain a competitive NCAA Division III competition schedule in collaboration with the Director of Athletics. Manage the program\u2019s budget with integrity and fiscal responsibility. Coordinate alumni engagement, fundraising initiatives, and community service activities. Collaborate with Sports Information and the Office of Communication and Marketing to promote the program\u2019s brand and presence. Ensure compliance with all NCAA Division III, Presidents\u2019 Athletic Conference (PAC), and institutional rules and guidelines. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree required; Master\u2019s degree preferred. Minimum of 2\u20133 years of successful coaching experience (lacrosse or related sport). Demonstrated competence in recruiting, program building, and student-athlete development. Strong commitment to the academic and personal development of student-athletes. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively in a team environment and demonstrate integrity in all aspects of coaching and administration. Performance Expectations: Head Coaches are expected to meet established performance standards that support the mission and sustainability of Thiel College Athletics. These expectations include: Achieving assigned recruiting and roster targets; Maintaining retention benchmarks; Fostering a positive student-athlete experience; Demonstrating competitive progress appropriate to program tenure; Engaging alumni, parents, community partners, and supporters; Contributing to program and departmental fundraising initiatives; and Supporting community engagement efforts. Head Coaches are also expected to develop and execute an annual program calendar that outlines: Recruiting activities Competition schedules Fundraising initiatives Alumni engagement Academic monitoring Team development plans Application Process: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should visit Thiel\u2019s employment site for more information (www.thiel.edu/employment-opportunities).  An application is available by clicking here .  A resume, reference information and cover letter should be attached within the application in a single PDF document with the applicant\u2019s last name as the file name. Materials will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. About the College Founded in 1866, Thiel College is an independent liberal arts college in western Pennsylvania, offering innovative undergraduate and graduate programs. Shaped by its Lutheran heritage, Thiel provides an accessible and inclusive learning environment and serves a diverse student population. The college has an active and supportive alumni base and maintains strong ongoing relationships within the local community. About the Area Greenville is located in northwestern Pennsylvania, a 90-minute drive from both Pittsburgh and Cleveland and a 40-minute drive from Youngstown, Ohio. Greenville and the surrounding areas have scenic parks, trails, and waterways for relaxing, hiking, camping, and boating. The area has a low cost of living, making it a desirable location for young professionals and growing families. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/digital-learning-coordinator-library": {"title": "Digital Learning Coordinator", "description": "Digital Learning Coordinator - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Digital Learning Coordinator Thiel College is seeking a dedicated educator to serve as our Digital Learning Coordinator. This is a full-time staff position, committed to the values of a liberal arts education and Thiel College's Mission to prepare students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. The Digital Learning Coordinator will work closely with faculty to develop curricula and assignments that help students develop research strategies, evaluate sources, and apply ethical information practices in the digital age. This position will also support faculty for instructional design and oversee the College\u2019s online course evaluation process, OCRA. The position offers an opportunity to work collaboratively with a variety of stakeholders to deepen engagement with the College and advance student learning. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Library and Information Science, Curriculum and Instruction, Instructional Design , or a related field At least three years of experience in a library, center of teaching and learning, or instructional design. Experience teaching information literacy, research methods, or related coursework Demonstrable record of effective communication and collaboration Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with assessment practices in higher education Experience developing curriculum aligned with institutional learning outcomes Essential Job Functions : Perform Library Instruction in classroom settings, especially for three courses comprising the First-Year experience: First-Year Seminar, College Writing, and Presentational Literacy Develop Presentation and Information Literacy syllabi designed to support student success and align with Thiel's all-college goals and mission Teach 1 section of Information Literacy per semester, based on enrollment needs Provide substantive feedback on student work and maintain regular office hours to support student development Support faculty development around instructional design and online teaching. Oversee the College\u2019s online course evaluation and approval process, OCRA. Work with the Associate Dean for Accreditation and Institutional Effectiveness to develop and integrate the assessment plan for information literacy into the overall institutional assessment plan Collaborate with department chairs and library faculty as appropriate Working Conditions: Heavy lifting up to 50lbs., pushing/pulling up to 50lbs., climbing, repeated overhead motion. Office hours may vary. Occasional evenings and weekends in a general office and campus environment. Safety/Training Requirements: Continuing education for topics relevant to the field. Periodic training on topics of nondiscrimination, prevention of harassment, prevention of sexual misconduct, cybersecurity, and other topics as required. General safety training and ergonomics training relevant to an office environment. About the College Founded in 1866, Thiel College is an independent liberal arts college in western Pennsylvania, offering innovative undergraduate and graduate programs. Shaped by its Lutheran heritage, Thiel provides an accessible and inclusive learning environment and serves a diverse student population. The college has an active and supportive alumni base and maintains strong ongoing relationships within the local community. About the Area Greenville is located in northwestern Pennsylvania, a 90-minute drive from both Pittsburgh and Cleveland and a 40-minute drive from Youngstown, Ohio. Greenville and the surrounding areas have scenic parks, trails, and waterways for relaxing, hiking, camping, and boating. The area has a low cost of living, making it a desirable location for young professionals and growing families. To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should visit Thiel\u2019s employment site for more information (www.thiel.edu/employment-opportunities).  An application is available by clicking here .  A resume, reference information and cover letter should be attached within the application in a single PDF document with the applicant\u2019s last name as the file name. Materials will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/golf-coach-pt-assistant": {"title": "Golf Coach - PT Assistant", "description": "Golf Coach - PT Assistant - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Golf Coach - PT Assistant Thiel College seeks an Assistant Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Golf Coach (PT). This position reports to the Head Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Golf Coach and the Director of Athletics. The selected candidate will assist the Head Coach in all aspects of the College\u2019s intercollegiate men\u2019s and women\u2019s golf programs while holistically developing student-athletes into leaders. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach and instruct student-athletes in the sport of golf as a primary coaching responsibility. Assist the Head Coach in all aspects of practice preparation, competition preparation, and program operations. Assist with the instruction and development of student-athletes in technical skills, course management, competitive preparation, and overall athletic development. Mentor and monitor student-athletes\u2019 academic progress. Evaluate student-athletes academically and athletically. Assist in planning and implementing pre- and post-workout programs. Recruit, retain, and graduate quality student-athletes for Thiel College and the men\u2019s and women\u2019s golf programs. Support assigned recruiting responsibilities, including prospect identification, communication, campus visits, follow-up, and other activities established by the Head Coach. Assist with fundraising activities and departmental fundraising initiatives. Assist with alumni, parent, community partner, and supporter engagement. Assist with community service planning and implementation. Serve as a gameday or event administrator when assigned. Assist with team travel, competition logistics, equipment, and other operational responsibilities as assigned. Follow all rules and guidelines established by NCAA Division III, the Presidents\u2019 Athletic Conference, and Thiel College. Perform other administrative and program responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Athletics and Head Coach. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree is required. Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred. Strong communication, organizational, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse populations. Ability and willingness to work evenings, weekends, and other hours necessary to support practices, competitions, recruiting, travel, and departmental responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications The successful candidate should: Candidates must be self-motivated Possess strong communication skills Have solid organizational, interpersonal, and leadership skills Work collaboratively and effectively as a member of the Athletic Department. The candidate must also strive for excellence and have pride in everything they do. Demonstrate a commitment to student-athlete development and the mission of NCAA Division III athletics. Performance Expectations Assistant Coaches are expected to work collaboratively with the Head Coach in meeting established performance standards that support the mission and sustainability of Thiel College Athletics. These expectations include: Achieving assigned recruiting and roster development targets. Supporting established student-athlete retention benchmarks. Fostering a positive and development-focused student-athlete experience. Contributing to competitive progress appropriate to the program\u2019s established goals. Engaging alumni, parents, community partners, and supporters. Contributing to program and departmental fundraising initiatives. Supporting community engagement and service efforts. Maintaining appropriate academic monitoring and supporting student-athlete academic success. Completing assigned administrative, compliance, recruiting, and operational responsibilities accurately and within established deadlines. Supporting the Head Coach in creating and maintaining sustainable men\u2019s and women\u2019s golf programs. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for following and actively supporting the Head Coach\u2019s established annual program calendar. The annual calendar should outline recruiting activities, fundraising initiatives, alumni engagement opportunities, academic monitoring strategies, community engagement, and other program priorities during the fall and spring semesters to support student-athlete retention, development, and success. The College evaluates performance using a comprehensive and holistic approach and is committed to supporting professional growth. When reasonable progress toward established expectations is not evident, next steps may include a performance improvement plan or probation and, when appropriate, non-renewal of the employment appointment, in accordance with College policies. Compliance and Professional Conduct Successful candidates must adhere to all NCAA, Presidents\u2019 Athletic Conference, and institutional guidelines, policies, and rules. The Assistant Coach is expected to demonstrate professional behavior, operate with integrity, and support the standards and expectations established by the Head Coach, Director of Athletics, and Thiel College. Position Classification This is a Casual Part-Time position with a $5,000 annual stipend. To Apply Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should visit Thiel\u2019s employment site for more information ( www.thiel.edu/employment-opportunities ).  An application is available by clicking here .  A resume, reference information, and cover letter should be attached within the application in a single PDF document with the applicant\u2019s last name as the file name. Materials will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. About Thiel College Thiel College is committed to attracting culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff dedicated to engaging students in a rich, fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel Athletics is guided by a commitment to excellence, leadership development, and the holistic growth of student-athletes, preparing them to reach their full potential in competition, academics, and life. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/maintenance-grounds-setup": {"title": "Maintenance", "description": "Maintenance - Grounds & Setup - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Maintenance - Grounds & Setup This position is dayshift (M-F), but may require some flexibility for occasional evenings and weekends.   This is a great role for working parents as shifts start early in the morning and end in the early afternoon. Thiel College offers a robust benefits package, including tuition remission.  Our engaging campus community is a family-friendly place to work as we support a safe, functional, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Thiel College is currently seeking motivated and qualified candidates for a full-time Maintenance Grounds and Setup role.  This position is responsible for performing various day-to-day groundskeeping and event setup services including, but not limited to, caring for lawns, hedges, mulch beds, and trees by mowing, edging, trimming, cleaning, raking, custodial duties, snow removal, transporting and setting up items as needed for campus events, both large and small.  This position is for (M-F) dayshift, but may require some flexibility or occasional evenings and weekends. Qualifications: Previous groundskeeping experience is preferred   Applicant should exhibit customer service skills with a professional, confidential, and positive personality, maintain a working knowledge of a wide range of vehicles, machinery, and equipment utilized in all areas of the physical plant. This position responds daily to work orders, emergency repairs, and campus departments/services, and operates college equipment and other off-road vehicles. Accountable for selected projects. The selected candidate will be required to perform other general maintenance duties as assigned. Thiel College Facilities is a team-working environment. Education and Experience: A high school diploma or equivalent At least two years of experience in facilities or building maintenance. Ability to read and interpret work orders and technical information Capacity to work independently as well as collaboratively. A valid driver\u2019s license Strong problem-solving skills Ability to perform the physical demands of the position while adhering to safety and regulatory standards are also required. Physical Requirements: Good physical condition, motor skills, hand and eye coordination, and manual dexterity. May be required to lift, push, or pull up to 70 pounds. May be required to crouch, kneel, bend, or stand for long periods. Capable of climbing at moderate heights. Possible exposure to chemical, mechanical, or electrical hazards, dust, fumes, and odorous working conditions. May be required to work outdoors in inclement weather. May be required to wear protective clothing or devices, such as goggles, gloves, masks or shields. Supervision: Supervises some student workers and/or provide functional guidance of support staff or other employees who work on a project or assignment on a temporary or intermittent basis. Safety/Training Requirements: Continuing education for topics relevant to the field. Periodic training on topics of nondiscrimination, prevention of harassment, prevention of sexual misconduct, and other topics as required. General safety training and ergonomics training relevant to an office environment. A post-job-offer physical exam and background check will be required (scheduled and paid by the College). Why Thiel? Thiel College offers a robust benefits package, including tuition remission.  Our engaging campus community is a friendly place to work.  Thiel College empowers individuals to reach their full potential by creating a diverse and inclusive learning environment that ensures educational excellence, stimulates global awareness, and promotes ethical leadership. In doing so, Thiel prepares students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should visit Thiel\u2019s employment site for more information (www.thiel.edu/employment-opportunities).  An application is available by clicking here .  A resume, reference information and cover letter should be attached within the application in a single PDF document with the applicant\u2019s last name as the file name. Materials will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/internship-and-assistant-mens-lacrosse-coach": {"title": "Internship and Assistant Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach", "description": "Internship and Assistant Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Internship and Assistant Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coach Thiel College seeks an Assistant Men\u2019s Lacrosse Coaching Intern. This position will report to the Head Lacrosse Coach and the Director of Athletics. The selected candidates will be responsible for assisting in all aspects of the college's intercollegiate Lacrosse program while holistically developing student-athletes to be leaders. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assist the Head Coach in      all aspects of practice and game preparation. Mentor student-athletes      and monitor their academic progress. Evaluate student-athletes      both academically and athletically. Ensure compliance with all      rules and regulations established by NCAA Division III, the Presidents\u2019      Athletic Conference, and Thiel College. Recruit, retain, and      support the graduation of quality student-athletes for Thiel College and      the athletic program. Assist in the planning and      implementation of pre- and post-workout programs. Support fundraising      initiatives and activities. Assist with the planning      and implementation of community service projects and events. Perform additional      administrative duties as assigned by the Head Coach and Director of      Athletics. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred. Strong communication, organizational, and leadership skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse populations. Preferred Qualifications Candidates must be self-motivated Possess strong communication skills Have solid organizational, interpersonal, and leadership skills The candidate must also strive for excellence and have pride in everything they do. Performance Expectations: Assistant Coaches are expected to work collaboratively with their head coach in meeting established performance standards that support the mission and sustainability of Thiel College Athletics. These expectations include achieving assigned recruiting and roster targets; maintaining retention benchmarks; fostering a positive student-athlete experience; demonstrating competitive progress appropriate to program tenure; engaging alumni, parents, community partners, and supporters; contributing to program and departmental fundraising initiatives; and supporting community engagement efforts. In addition, Assistant Coaches are responsible to follow and actively support the head coach\u2019s established annual program calendar that outlines recruiting activities, fundraising initiatives, alumni engagement events, and academic monitoring strategies during the fall and spring semesters to support student-athlete retention and success. The College evaluates performance using a comprehensive, holistic approach and is committed to supporting growth. When reasonable progress is not evident, next steps may include a performance improvement plan or probation, and, when appropriate, non-renewal of employment appointment, in accordance with College policies. Successful candidates must adhere to all NCAA, conference, and institutional guidelines, policies, and rules. Demonstrate professional behavior while operating with integrity. This is a 10-month position with a $10,000 stipend and includes housing, meals, cell phone, as well as an athletic professional development class provided by the College. To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should visit Thiel\u2019s employment site for more information (www.thiel.edu/employment-opportunities).  An application is available by clicking here .  A resume, reference information and cover letter should be attached within the application in a single PDF document with the applicant\u2019s last name as the file name. Materials will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. About Thiel College: Thiel College is committed to attracting culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff dedicated to engaging students in a rich, fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel Athletics is guided by a commitment to excellence, leadership development, and the holistic growth of student-athletes, preparing them to reach their full potential in competition, academics, and life. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/professor-of-united-states-history-tenure-track": {"title": "Professor of United States History", "description": "Professor of United States History - Tenure Track - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Professor of United States History - Tenure Track The Department of History at Thiel College invites applications for a tenure-track position in United States History. Teaching responsibilities will include American surveys and upper-division courses in United States History. Areas of specialization are open, but preference will be given to candidates whose teaching and professional interests support the preparation of future history educators and the use of technology to enhance history instruction, historical research, and student learning. Candidates should have an interest in joining an undergraduate department where teaching in a small classroom environment is emphasized. Expectations include a 4/4 teaching load, developing engaging pedagogy, openness to interdisciplinary courses, advising, and active involvement in the campus community. Candidates must have a Doctorate in History; candidates currently completing doctoral work will also be considered. A dedicated passion for helping students reach their full potential in a supportive and inclusive, diverse environment is essential to this position. Responsibilities include teaching, advising, student supervision, and professional development. While Thiel College gives highest priority to teaching effectiveness, faculty are expected to remain current in the field through professional development opportunities such as attendance at related conferences, research, or other scholarly activities. A comprehensive employee benefit package, including research support and a sabbatical program, is provided. Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Applicants should: Submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae and list of references (all these materials should be attached in a single PDF document using candidate\u2019s name as the document title) by clicking here . Additional required materials, including transcripts, sample syllabi for both a survey and an upper-division U.S. history course, and summaries of recent teaching evaluations, if available, should be sent in PDF format to employment@thiel.edu (preferred option).  These items may also be mailed to Jennifer Clark, Director of Human Resources, Thiel College, 75 College Avenue, Greenville, PA. 16125. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. About Thiel College Thiel College is an independent liberal arts college rooted in the Lutheran tradition. Thiel College empowers individuals to reach their full potential by creating a diverse and inclusive learning environment that ensures educational excellence, stimulates global awareness, and promotes ethical leadership. In doing so, Thiel prepares students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. About the Area Greenville is in northwestern Pennsylvania, a 90-minute drive from both Pittsburgh and Cleveland and a 40-minute drive from Youngstown, Ohio. Greenville and the surrounding areas have scenic parks, trails, and waterways for relaxing, hiking, camping, and boating. The area has a low cost of living, making it a desirable location for young professionals and growing families. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/adjunct-instructors-in-math": {"title": "Adjunct Instructors in Math", "description": "Adjunct Instructors in Math - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Adjunct Instructors in Math Thiel College invites applications from qualified individuals to join our adjunct instructor pool in the Department of Math and Computer Science. We are actively building a roster of adjunct faculty available to teach on a course-by-course basis in the Spring 2027 semester and beyond. Two introductory quantitative reasoning courses are in need of coverage in spring 2027. Qualifications A master\u2019s      degree in math, education, or a related field is required. A minimum      of two years of teaching experience is preferred. In-person      instruction at our Greenville, Pennsylvania campus is preferred; however,      remote options including synchronous online delivery are available for      qualified candidates. Why Thiel? Thiel College is an independent liberal arts college rooted in the Lutheran tradition. Thiel College empowers individuals to reach their full potential by creating a diverse and inclusive learning environment that ensures educational excellence, stimulates global awareness, and promotes ethical leadership. In doing so, Thiel prepares students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. To apply, submit a letter of interest, CV, and contact information for three professional references as a single PDF document (titled with your last name) by clicking here . Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Visit www.thiel.edu to learn more about Thiel College. Thiel is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage students through rich curricular and cocurricular experiences. EOE Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"}, "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/clinical-nursing-adjunct": {"title": "Clinical Adjunct Nursing Instructor", "description": "Clinical Adjunct Nursing Instructor - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Clinical Adjunct Nursing Instructor Thiel College seeks vibrant candidates to serve as adjunct faculty in our baccalaureate level Nursing program. Faculty collaborate with the Program Director to support the program\u2019s mission and ensure compliance with CCNE accreditation standards.  A dedicated passion for helping students reach their full potential in a supportive and inclusive environment is essential to this position. Responsibilities primarily include teaching and student supervision. Qualifications: Teaching in a higher education setting is preferred but not required; effective communication and collaborative skills in a team-oriented environment and a history of successful time management Med/Surg nursing experience required Psych or pediatric nursing experience preferred, other specialty areas welcome A Master\u2019s degree in Nursing from an accredited program is required; Ph.D or D.N.P preferred. Candidates who are near completion of their Master\u2019s degree in Nursing will also be considered Must have current unencumbered RN license in Pennsylvania Knowledge of BSN-level assessment of clinical education preferred Essential Functions: Teach assigned courses within our Nursing Program to meet lab and clinical needs Contribute to curriculum development to ensure student learning objectives are met Monitor student progress and contribute to remediation when necessary Assist with CCNE accreditation activities Maintain licensure and/or certification To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should please submit a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for three professional references by clicking here . All application materials should be attached in a single PDF document using candidate\u2019s name (Lname, Fname) as the document title.  For additional information, please contact Dr. Debra Wallace dwallace@thiel.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until positions are filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links \u00d7 Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Bu